hree points.\n\nCognetti's fundraising has produced a cash advantage, roughly $3.4 million on hand to Bresnahan's $2.6 million, and the Giffords PAC has put about $850,000 into ads attacking the incumbent on gun policy and stock trading. Bresnahan's counterattacks on Cognetti's tax record have drawn mixed fact-checks. The district's fundamentals keep the race genuinely competitive, but money, environment and outside spending point modestly toward the challenger.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5916, "margin": 1.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6449, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6453, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6734, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.617, "margin": 2.4}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6201, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6673, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6811, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6435, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6763, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6884, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6826, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6869, "margin": 2.5}]}